CloudBurrow patch 62 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1547).

The bug: a GEOGRAPHY that a streamed row (tabledata.insertAll) or a JSON or
CSV load gave as text, WKT or GeoJSON, was bound as that text, and the
engine stored it as a STRING: ST_ASTEXT, ST_X and every other geography
function of the column failed "expected GEOGRAPHY, got value.StringValue".
BigQuery loads a GEOGRAPHY from WKT, WKB or GeoJSON text
(https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/geospatial-data). The patch binds a
non-REPEATED GEOGRAPHY column's value through ST_GEOGFROM(CAST(? AS STRING)), which reads WKT
and GeoJSON into a geography, in Repository.addTableRows, which every write
of rows goes through. A GEOGRAPHY inside a RECORD or a REPEATED one is left
as it was. server/geography_values_test.go fails without the patch and
passes with it.

